  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>signtest</keyword>
  <short_description>Sign test.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>p = signtest(x)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>p = signtest(x, y)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>p = signtest(x, m)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>p = signtest(x, y, Name, Value)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[p, h, stats] = signtest(...)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>signtest</b> performs a sign test for a median or paired difference. If <b>y</b> is omitted, values of <b>x</b> are tested against zero. If <b>y</b> is a scalar, values of <b>x</b> are tested against that scalar.</p>
    <p>Name-value arguments include <b>Alpha</b>, <b>Method</b>, and <b>Tail</b>. Zero differences and <b>NaN</b> values are omitted.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[x = [1 2 -3 4 -5];
[p, h, stats] = signtest(x)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
